<p>A sequence similarity network (SSN) allows for visualization of relationships among protein sequences. In SSNs, the most related proteins are grouped together in clusters. The Enzyme Similarity Tool (EFI-EST) makes it possible to easily generate SSNs. <a href="http://www.cytoscape.org/">Cytoscape</a> is used to explore SSNs.</p>

<p><a href="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/search/sequence-search">InterProScan sequence search</a> can be used to find matches within the InterPro database for a given sequence.</p>

<p>Information on Pfam families and clans and InterPro family sizes is available on the <a href="{{ path('family_list') }}">Family Information page</a>.</p>
